<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main class="flex-grow py-12 sm:py-20">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="border-b-2 border-tbf-navy pb-8 mb-12">
      <span class="tbf-category-badge text-xs">Manifesto & Masthead</span>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-tbf-navy mt-2 leading-tight">
        Chronicling the Architects of Modern India.
      </h1>
      <p class="font-sans text-lg sm:text-xl text-gray-600 font-medium leading-relaxed mt-4">
        The Bombay Forum (TBF) is a premium editorial journal covering business, wealth, luxury, and culture in the world’s most dynamic economy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- The Manifesto -->
    <div class="space-y-6 text-base sm:text-lg text-gray-800 font-sans leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        India in 2026 is undergoing the most consequential economic and cultural expansion in modern history. From the sovereign balance sheets of Nariman Point to the AI laboratories of Bengaluru and the creative studios of Bandra, a generational cohort of founders, operators, and cultural pioneers is rewiring the subcontinent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Yet mainstream media coverage remains caught in a false dichotomy: breathless PR hype on one end, and commoditised clickbait on the other. <strong>The Bombay Forum was founded to build something enduring: high-conviction reporting, authoritative analysis, and intellectual depth.</strong>
      </p>

      <blockquote class="tbf-pullquote">
        We assume our readers are intelligent, ambitious, and already informed. Our role is to deliver perspective over noise.
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-tbf-navy pt-8">Our Editorial Principles</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-4 pt-2">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <strong class="text-tbf-teal text-xl font-serif">01.</strong>
          <div><strong>Original Analysis:</strong> We publish thesis-driven reporting on people and companies actually building things, not dressed-up press releases.</div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <strong class="text-tbf-teal text-xl font-serif">02.</strong>
          <div><strong>Editorial Rigour:</strong> Precision over sensationalism. Zero exclamation marks, zero clickbait, and numbers over empty adjectives.</div>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <strong class="text-tbf-teal text-xl font-serif">03.</strong>
          <div><strong>The Soul of Maximum City:</strong> Bombay is our physical and spiritual anchor—a city of uncompromising grit, historic trade, and boundless cultural vitality.</div>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <!-- Masthead Section -->
      <div class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-tbf-border">
        <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-tbf-navy mb-6">Editorial Masthead</h3>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm">
          <div class="p-4 bg-surface border-l-2 border-tbf-navy">
            <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold text-gray-500 block">Editorial Direction</span>
            <div class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-tbf-navy mt-1">Editor-in-Chief & Desk</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-gray-600">editorial@thebombayforum.com</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 bg-surface border-l-2 border-tbf-navy">
            <span class="text-[10px] uppercase font-bold text-gray-500 block">Brand Partnerships</span>
            <div class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-tbf-navy mt-1">TBF Spotlight Desk</div>
            <div class="text-xs text-gray-600">partnerships@thebombayforum.com</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
